    Bug 1787104 - Allow messages.import() to directly import into IMAP folders. r=aleca

    The missing link to get `messages.import()` on IMAP folders working is:
    ```
    folder.updateFolder(null);
    ```
    This will trigger some IMAP magic to make the newly added message appear
    in the folder and to trigger the `MailServices.mfn.msgAdded` listener.

    Another issue was that some protocol implementations did not always
    fire the `nsIMsgCopyServiceListener.setMessageKey()` callback. Instead
    of trying to fix the implementation, we simply look for messages with
    the expected headerMessageId, if we did not get notified about the
    messageKey in time.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D225342

